 "teaches": [
  "A formula, not a mesh: {\"fn\": \"exp(-(x^2 + y^2) / (2 * s^2))\", \"x\": [-3, 3], \"vars\": [{\"name\": \"s\", \"value\": \"@sigma\", \"min\": 0.4, \"max\": 2}]}; the player evaluates it on a 44 x 44 grid every frame",
  "vars with min and max: the server sizes the z axis for every σ the slider can reach (here 0..1, the peak is always 1)",
  "The slider comes before the chart in the document: from the slider on, @sigma is the slider's live value, so the surface reshapes while dragging",
  "Five height bands (light to dark blue) are five copies of the mesh, each clamped below its band's top; a grey skirt closes the sides; mono is a hidden-line wireframe"
 ],
 "pitfalls": [
  "3D support has not landed in androidx yet (coming): this plays in the C++ and TypeScript players only. Don't use it for a screen that must play on Android today",
  "The TypeScript player's MeshExpression (players/typescript/src/core/operations/d3/MeshExpression.ts) reads its grid parameters as raw float bits, so today no meshExpression3D surface draws in the web player: the box, labels and slider show with an empty floor. Fixing gridCount and paramsFor to read the bits as floats makes it match the C++ render"
 ],
 "java_difference": "3D operations: not in the Java JSON parser or androidx remote-core yet; 3D support has not landed in androidx yet (coming); plays in the C++ and TypeScript players",
 "inputs": {
  "variables": {
   "sigma": {
    "min": 0.4,
    "max": 2
   }
  }
 },
